; once-hold-band.fk — a top-level let binds a VALUE, not a recipe for one.
; Witnessed 2026-09-02 before the heal: fkwu spliced a top-level let's
; initializer NODE into every reference site, so each read re-walked the
; whole build (call-by-name — "built" printed three times, the Go arm
; printed once). The once-hold (tag 190) gives every reference one shared
; hold node whose first read computes and holds.
;
; The witness is an EFFECT count, not a heat read: the held value's
; initializer appends one line to a scratch file per build. Three
; references to HELD leave ONE line under the once-hold; call-by-name
; would leave three. The band is TOP-LEVEL on purpose — HELD must be a
; top-level const for the hold to apply and for `use` to see it (a defn
; frame cannot close over a do-local let).
;
; The held value is a melt root: fk_melt copies it and fk_smelt marks it,
; so a melt between two reads builds nothing again. The churn below keeps
; its loop on the walker (a clock in its compare), whose conses melt: a lane
; leaf grows the heap in place instead. The mark is named by the kernel's
; pid, so a let read again after a melt would write to the same file.
;
; bits:  1 the held value reads through three references (sum 21)
;        2 the initializer ran exactly ONCE (one line written)
;        4 the old call-by-name count (three) is absent
;        8 after a walked churn of 20,000 conses, which melts the heap, a
;          fourth read still finds one line
; Verdict 15.
; PROOF LEVEL: FKWU + GO — go answers 7 too (witnessed 2026-09-03; host-exec pf-arm-mask 9). The once-hold is fkwu's const-hold; the sibling
; arms build top-level lets once already (witnessed by cost, 2026-09-02).
; preludes: form-stdlib/core.fk
(defn ohb-build (m) (do (let e (host-exec (str_concat "echo built >> " m) "")) (list 7)))
(let OHB-MARK (str_concat "/tmp/once-hold-band-" (host-exec "printf %s $PPID" "")))
(let OHB-CLEAN (host-exec (str_concat "rm -f " OHB-MARK) ""))
(let OHB-HELD (ohb-build OHB-MARK))
(defn ohb-use () (head OHB-HELD))
(let OHB-SUM (add (ohb-use) (add (ohb-use) (ohb-use))))
(let OHB-COUNT (host-exec (str_concat "grep -c built " (str_concat OHB-MARK " | tr -d '\n'")) ""))
(defn ohb-churn (n xs) (if (lt (host_monotonic_ms) 0) xs (if (le n 0) (len xs) (ohb-churn (sub n 1) (cons n xs)))))
(let OHB-AFTER (add (ohb-churn 20000 (list)) (ohb-use)))
(let OHB-COUNT2 (host-exec (str_concat "grep -c built " (str_concat OHB-MARK " | tr -d '\n'")) ""))
(let OHB-SWEEP (host-exec (str_concat "rm -f " OHB-MARK) ""))
(add (if (eq OHB-SUM 21) 1 0)
     (add (if (str_eq OHB-COUNT "1") 2 0)
          (add (if (str_eq OHB-COUNT "3") 0 4)
               (if (if (eq OHB-AFTER 20007) (str_eq OHB-COUNT2 "1") false) 8 0))))
